Sentiment Analysis on Twitter using Machine Learning

A Machine Learning project that analyzes sentiments (Positive, Negative, Neutral) from Twitter data using Natural Language Processing (NLP) techniques.

Project Overview :

This project focuses on building a Sentiment Analysis model that classifies tweets based on the emotion or sentiment expressed in the text.
With the rapid growth of social media, analyzing public opinion has become crucial for businesses, political campaigns, and brand monitoring. This project demonstrates how machine learning and NLP techniques can be used to extract meaningful insights from unstructured text data.

Objective :

1.Preprocess and clean Twitter text data
2.Perform Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
3.Convert text into numerical format using vectorization techniques
4.Train machine learning models
5.Evaluate model performance
6.Predict sentiment for new tweets

Technologies & Tools Used :

Python,
Pandas & NumPy,
Matplotlib & Seaborn,
Scikit-learn,
NLTK,
TF-IDF / Count Vectorizer
